# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'core-fellowship: add configurable block number provider'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `pallet-core-fellowship` now has a configurable `BlockNumberProvider` instead of always using
      the local `frame_system` block number. The pallet's timing storage and checks for promotion,
      demotion, proof, and offboarding periods now use the configured provider's block-number type.

      Runtimes that need the previous behavior can set `BlockNumberProvider` to
      `frame_system::Pallet`. Runtimes that change provider domains should include the provided
      `MigrateV1ToV2` migration with a `ConvertBlockNumber` implementation to translate stored
      local block numbers into the new provider's block-number domain.

      Collectives Westend now configures the Fellowship and Ambassador core-fellowship instances to
      use `cumulus_pallet_parachain_system::RelaychainDataProvider`, with a runtime migration that
      translates existing timing storage from local parachain block numbers to relay-chain block
      numbers.

  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      Collectives Westend Fellowship and Ambassador promotion, demotion, proof, and offboarding
      timing is now evaluated using relay-chain block numbers. Existing timing-related storage is
      translated during the runtime upgrade.

migrations:
  runtime:
    - reference: pallet_core_fellowship::migration::MigrateV1ToV2
      description: |
        Converts `pallet-core-fellowship` `Params` duration fields and `Member` timestamp fields
        from the previous local `frame_system` block-number domain into the configured
        `BlockNumberProvider` domain. Collectives Westend applies this to both Fellowship and
        Ambassador core-fellowship instances.

crates:
  - name: pallet-core-fellowship
    bump: major
  - name: collectives-westend-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: kitchensink-runtime
    bump: patch
